  "answer": "This has been reported before. It looks like the pane-split animation, not a DWM/MPO regression. When you split a pane, the new pane's backdrop is briefly transparent while the animation runs, so whatever is behind the window shows through for a frame or two. That matches your symptoms. terminal#19250 describes the same thing: Shift+Alt+D on build 26100, with content behind the window flashing until the new pane renders. It was closed as a duplicate of terminal#12334, 'The open pane animation background is transparent'. terminal#7365 describes the underlying cause: the parent grid is resized immediately, and the backdrop is visible while the new pane slides in. The maintainers said terminal#12334 is not likely to be fixed soon, because a real fix would need a different UI framework. I found no workaround in the archive tickets. Your guess about the 24H2 Independent Flip regression (terminal#19010) is a separate issue. In that ticket, Terminal falls back to Composed Flip and the reporter saw only extra input latency, not a flash. Please add your details to terminal#12334 instead of opening a new issue. You could also try turning off pane animations, but none of these tickets confirms that this removes the flash."
 },
